2026-10-28T17:40:05.7812234Z {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FpHPEtDT1Xv3AVZ5WC4ZFe","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Comment format\n2\t\n3\tOne comment per issue, at most 1,500 characters. Write plain, friendly English. Start with\n4\t`Thanks for the report, @<author>.` and give the single reason for the comment. Then end with\n5\tthis exact footer line, on its own line after a blank line:\n6\t\n7\t```\n8\t_Automated first-pass triage. A maintainer will review this issue and make every decision on it._\n9\t```\n10\t\n11\tRules that `validate_plan.py` checks:\n12\t\n13\t- Mention only the issue author.\n14\t- Link only https URLs on github.com, discuss.hashicorp.com, registry.terraform.io,\n15\t  developer.hashicorp.com or www.hashicorp.com.\n16\t- Reference only issues that the duplicate search returned, by their `ref` (`#123`, or `owner/repo#123` for an\n17\t  issue in another repository), never by URL.\n18\t- Do not claim to have closed, removed, assigned or prioritised anything, and do not mention any approval.\n19\t\n20\t## Templates\n21\t\n22\tAdapt the wording to the issue. Keep the structure.\n23\t\n24\t**Possible duplicate**\n25\t\n26\t```\n27\tThanks for the report, @<author>. This looks like it may be the same request as <ref> (<short title>).\n28\tIf it is, please add a 👍 and any extra details there, so the discussion stays in one place.\n29\tIf it is different, a short note on how it differs will help the maintainers.\n30\t\n31\t_Automated first-pass triage. A maintainer will review this issue and make every decision on it._\n32\t```\n33\t\n34\t**Missing information**\n35\t\n36\t```\n37\tThanks for the report, @<author>. To reproduce this, the maintainers will need:\n38\t\n39\t- <missing item 1>\n40\t- <missing item 2>\n41\t\n42\tCould you add these to the issue description?\n43\t\n44\t_Automated first-pass triage. A maintainer will review this issue and make every decision on it._\n45\t```\n46\t\n47\t**Outdated version, or a newer release with a fix for this resource**\n48\t\n49\t```\n50\tThanks for the report, @<author>. You are on provider v<reported>, and the latest release is v<latest>.\n51\t[v<newer_fixes[0]> includes fixes for `<resource>`.]\n52\tCould you check whether this still happens on v<latest>? If it does, please add the output from that run.\n53\t\n54\t_Automated first-pass triage. A maintainer will review this issue and make every decision on it._\n55\t```\n56\t\n57\t**Wrong venue** (question, or a Terraform core problem)\n58\t\n59\t```\n60\tThanks for the question, @<author>. GitHub issues here are for provider bugs and feature requests.\n61\tUsage questions get faster answers on the community forum: https://discuss.hashicorp.com/c/terraform-providers/tf-aws\n62\t\n63\t_Automated first-pass triage. A maintainer will review this issue and make every decision on it._\n64\t```\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5c38c65-79d7-447f-b7a8-e401c07ed13c","uuid":"2eb95249-e9d1-4c3d-ac11-5c79a8d52737","timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:40:05.768Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/runner/work/cs467-as3-triage-agent/cs467-as3-triage-agent/.claude/skills/issue-triage/references/comment-format.md","content":"# Comment format\n\nOne comment per issue, at most 1,500 characters. Write plain, friendly English. Start with\n`Thanks for the report, @<author>.` and give the single reason for the comment. Then end with\nthis exact footer line, on its own line after a blank line:\n\n```\n_Automated first-pass triage. A maintainer will review this issue and make every decision on it._\n```\n\nRules that `validate_plan.py` checks:\n\n- Mention only the issue author.\n- Link only https URLs on github.com, discuss.hashicorp.com, registry.terraform.io,\n  developer.hashicorp.com or www.hashicorp.com.\n- Reference only issues that the duplicate search returned, by their `ref` (`#123`, or `owner/repo#123` for an\n  issue in another repository), never by URL.\n- Do not claim to have closed, removed, assigned or prioritised anything, and do not mention any approval.\n\n## Templates\n\nAdapt the wording to the issue. Keep the structure.\n\n**Possible duplicate**\n\n```\nThanks for the report, @<author>. This looks like it may be the same request as <ref> (<short title>).\nIf it is, please add a 👍 and any extra details there, so the discussion stays in one place.\nIf it is different, a short note on how it differs will help the maintainers.\n\n_Automated first-pass triage. A maintainer will review this issue and make every decision on it._\n```\n\n**Missing information**\n\n```\nThanks for the report, @<author>. To reproduce this, the maintainers will need:\n\n- <missing item 1>\n- <missing item 2>\n\nCould you add these to the issue description?\n\n_Automated first-pass triage. A maintainer will review this issue and make every decision on it._\n```\n\n**Outdated version, or a newer release with a fix for this resource**\n\n```\nThanks for the report, @<author>. You are on provider v<reported>, and the latest release is v<latest>.\n[v<newer_fixes[0]> includes fixes for `<resource>`.]\nCould you check whether this still happens on v<latest>? If it does, please add the output from that run.\n\n_Automated first-pass triage. A maintainer will review this issue and make every decision on it._\n```\n\n**Wrong venue** (question, or a Terraform core problem)\n\n```\nThanks for the question, @<author>. GitHub issues here are for provider bugs and feature requests.\nUsage questions get faster answers on the community forum: https://discuss.hashicorp.com/c/terraform-providers/tf-aws\n\n_Automated first-pass triage. A maintainer will review this issue and make every decision on it._\n```\n","numLines":65,"startLine":1,"totalLines":65}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FpHPEtDT1Xv3AVZ5WC4ZFe","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
